Built stdlib-only compress.py with mixed-radix encoding for structured records and an LZMA fallback for other input. Both requested CLI commands work, and decompression needs no original corpus. The 44,267-byte corpus compresses to 16,772 bytes—a 62.1117% reduction, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. Verified byte-identical restoration through the CLI and passed 37 additional edge-case/randomized round trips. Registered python3 fitness.py; its repeated, verified workload runs for at least 0.4 seconds, and the assay accepted the improved score with zero spread.